    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0109" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg27"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Motley</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 148.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 13, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and have read with deep
                    interest your despatches from No. 101, of April 30, to No. 106, of the 8th
                    ultimo. Your accounts of the feeling with which the news of the assassination of
                    the late President of the United States was received throughout the Austrian
                    empire, as well as elsewhere in Germany, are very gratifying. Your own
                    proceedings upon the case are approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Lothrop Motley</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Vienna.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
